The recipe (shared C++20 SystemC 3.0.1 + CCI, FastSim against them, vsim
modules told which SystemC, LD_PRELOAD of the engine) is in
`/home/nick/work/fastsim_v3/andesim/PORTING.md` (branch `andesim`).

Environment used on 2026-09-11:
- vsim modules build in podman `localhost/andescycle-dev:v0.16-17-g03dfe23`
  (host GCC 16 cannot compile vendored scc/LIEF): mounts `-v <vsim>:/work`
  `-v <fastsim_v3>:/fastsim` `-v <scratch>:/sp`; build dir is `<vsim>/build`
  (configured inside the container with `-DFASTSIM_DIR=/fastsim
  -DFASTSIM_LUA_INCLUDE=/sp/luainc -DFASTSIM_SYSTEMC_LIB=/sp/sc-shared/lib/libsystemc.so
  -DFASTSIM_CCI_LIB=/sp/cci-shared/lib/libcci.so`). Run:
  `podman run --rm -v ... -w /work IMAGE cmake --build build --target VsimCore_ax45mpv_premium`.
- Building `VsimCore_<cpu>` also generates `VsimCore_<cpu>.lua` and
  `VsimCore_<cpu>.qemu.cfg` beside it (`cmake/core_description.py`, from the
  RTL config header). The platform Lua loads them from ANDESIM_MODULES; the
  module refuses a description of another build.
- The shared SystemC/CCI, the FastSim build (`fsbuild/multi_arch_toplevel`,
  modules in `fsbuild/install/lib`) and Lua headers lived in that session's
  scratchpad under /tmp -- NOT persistent. A new session must rebuild them
  per PORTING.md before running the demos.
- Host unit tests: `cmake --build <vsim>/build-utest --target check` (GCC 16;
  30 tests incl. the Python generator tests).
- Test/demo env vars: FASTSIM_BIN, FASTSIM_MODULE_DIR, VSIM_CORE_SO (no .so),
  LD_LIBRARY_PATH (shared SystemC/CCI), FIXTURE_DIR; fixtures in
  `/home/nick/work/andesim/tests/fixtures` (old repo, read-only). A scratch
  `tmp/ae350_env.sh` in fastsim_v3 exported them for this session.

